{
  "_comment": [
    "The work a part can have done on it to take its mileage off (see docs/modding.md, \"rebuilds.json\"). A job is for the",
    "parts of its kinds (work_order.json's) or of its groups (part_groups.json's shelves). way: kit (the player's own work)",
    "or exchange (swapped at the parts counter for a rebuilt one, the old part the core). restores: the condition the part",
    "is in after it, 0 to 1 (a kit is not a new part); min_wear: a part worn below it is too far gone for the job (it wants",
    "a machine shop); cost: the kit or the rebuilt unit, a share of the part's new price, never less than cost_at_least",
    "dollars; minutes: the work, or the trip to the counter; off: done with the part off the car and off any other part",
    "(on the shelf, or the engine on the stand); bare: done with nothing mounted on it; fixes_damage: takes its damage off",
    "too. The player reads rebuild.<id> in the text, else name. A mod's job of the same id takes the place of this one,",
    "whole; \"disabled\": true takes it out."
  ],
